📄 Page 5. Report Strategy
🧾 Report behavior

The reporting implementation was designed to support both:

local execution
remote Jenkins execution

while using different report roots if necessary.

Main reporting goals
show test steps from JiraReportSteps
keep the full stack trace only in View full error
show only a short failure summary outside the expandable section
attach one failure evidence image per failed test case
resolve different report paths for local and remote runs
keep the HTML layout stable
✅ Rules for the HTML report
Steps section

The steps must display what was logged by JiraReportSteps.

They must not display the raw exception text inside the step list.

Step status rules
passed step = green
failed step = red
steps not executed after a failure = blocked, yellow
Visual Error Log rules

Outside the expandable area:

show only the short summary
stop at the intended short text boundary

Inside View full error:

show the complete error log and stack trace
Evidence rules
one failure image per failed test case
show only evidence related to the selected test case
do not show evidence from other test cases
support different image roots for local and remote environments
📄 Page 6. Local and Remote Differences
🖥️ Local environment

Typical characteristics:

runs from local Katalon Studio
reports under local workspace path
user may have multiple monitors
screenshot should preferably capture only one relevant screen
🖥️ Remote Jenkins environment

Typical characteristics:

runs through visible scheduled tasks
reports under Jenkins workspace
screenshot path differs from local
full desktop capture may be acceptable when needed
⚠️ Why path resolution matters

The evidence and logo issues came from the fact that:

local and remote report roots are not always identical
the image file may exist in a different folder depending on the execution mode
logo and evidence lookup must not assume a single fixed path

That is why the report builder must resolve:

current report folder
evidence folder
logo location

based on the actual execution environment.

