📄 Page 9. How to Chain Pipelines Safely
🔗 Goal

One pipeline may schedule the next pipeline after finishing.

Important rule

The current execution must be completely stopped before the next pipeline is scheduled.

That is why cleanup happens first, and only then the next job is triggered.

✅ Correct approach
First

Stop:

scheduled tasks
WinAppDriver
Katalon processes
Then

Schedule the next Jenkins job with:

build job: NEXT_JOB,
      wait: false,
      propagate: false

This means:

current job does not wait for the next one to finish
current job ends normally
next job starts as a new separate execution
❌ What must be avoided

Do not keep the first pipeline hanging while waiting for the second.

Do not trigger the next job before cleanup.

Do not let both suites overlap in the same desktop session.

📄 Page 10. Reusable Pattern for All Future Pipelines
🧩 Standard file set per suite

For every new suite, follow this model:

Jenkins
